So Truman was president and he wanted to have a mission to help Japan rebuild

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.000
He was aware of some of the work that Deming had done and invited Deming to come to Japan

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:23.000
And help in the re-establishing and manufacturing there

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.000
The Japanese really took to it, and they really embraced it

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:36.000
And so the shift was from the US to Japan, and some of the more important ones

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:44.000
Kauru Ishikawa and Shogyo Shingo and Genichi Taguchi

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.000
And there's others as well, but those are some of the ones that were more outstanding

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:03.000
And then the revival, then they realized, because Japan began to manufacture such outstanding quality products that

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:10.000
That the US was starting to lose market share. And so then they got interested in it and

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:18.000
And they called back many of these people like Duran and Deming to come back and help here in the US

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:32.000
And they did reform generally manufacturing here in the US so that they could begin to have parity. Of course, they've never completely overcome the gap that was created

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.000
People today

